<h1 style=3D"font-size:26px;font-weight:normal;">Werkraum Journal: August</h1>
<p>Dear Anna Weber,</p>
<p>This month, we take you behind the scenes of our furniture conservation wo=
rkshop, where careful observation comes before any intervention.</p>
<h2 style=3D"font-size:20px;">A chair, closely observed</h2>
<p>Curator Lotte Kern describes the restoration of a bentwood reading chair, =
tracing the decisions that shape its treatment: how to assess worn joints, di=
stinguish signs of use from damage, and preserve the character of the origina=
l finish.</p>
<p>The workshop offers a quieter perspective on the collection. Small details=
=E2=80=94a softened edge, an old repair, a change in the grain=E2=80=94can re=
veal how furniture was made and lived with.</p>
<p>We hope this glimpse into conservation encourages you to look a little mor=
e closely during your next visit.</p>
<p style=3D"margin-top:28px;">Warm regards,<br>The Werkraum Museum team</p>
